@@ -70,6 +70,22 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Use it when you want raw text output without Rich's formatting.
+
+``out`` does the following:
+
+- Writes the text without pretty printing, so containers are written as their string conversion.
+- Does not wrap or crop the text to the console width.
+- Does not interpret markup or replace emoji codes.
+- Applies highlighting by default. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+- Applies a basic style if you pass ``style``.
+
+Output from ``out`` still goes through the normal print path, so render hooks, buffering, and capture work as they do for :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print`.
+
+
